.TH MINI-BROWSER 1 "October 2026" "Mini Browser 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mini-browser \- a small native GNOME web browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mini-browser
.RI [ --agent ] " [" URL " or " "search terms" ]...
.br
.B mini-browser agent
.RI [ --socket " PATH] " COMMAND " ..."
.br
.B mini-browser mcp
.RI [ --socket " PATH]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mini Browser opens one page per resizable portrait window, with a native
GNOME header bar and sandboxed Chromium web content. Each command-line argument opens a separate window.
Quote search terms containing spaces. Without arguments, the start page opens.
It contains an address/search field and tiles for recently opened sites.
The header bar's main menu opens Settings, including Chrome data import.
Its Home button is always available; Back returns to the previous page when available.
Website links requesting another
tab or window open in the current window.
.PP
Audio and video layouts hide the title bar; move to the top edge or press F10
to reveal it. Video windows initially match the video's aspect ratio.
Choose Full page from the layout menu or press Escape to restore the page layout.
.PP
The pin button before the layout button keeps the window above other windows.
An active pin uses the theme accent color; an inactive pin uses an outlined icon.
Audio and video modes enable pinning by default; Full page restores the previous
pin setting. Pinning requires the bundled Mini Browser Pin GNOME Shell extension.
After installation, log out and back in, then run
.B gnome-extensions enable mini-browser-pin@io.github.stone
once. The pin button offers Enable Pinning and setup instructions if the
extension is unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application version.
.TP
.B \-\-agent
Enable private same-user agent control and keep running after the last window
closes. Use mini-browser agent stop or Quit to stop the application.
.SH AGENT CONTROL
mini-browser agent --help lists JSON control commands. Commands include list,
open, add-app, apps, remove-app, navigate, close, snapshot, click, fill, press, eval, screenshot, resize,
inspect, native-click, native-fill, action, cdp, tools, call, and stop. Page commands use
the numeric page ID returned by list or open. Navigation is asynchronous.
.PP
mini-browser agent add-app URL --title NAME saves a persistent Home tile without
opening the website or changing history. URL must be a full HTTP(S) address.
The title is optional. Repeated URLs update the existing tile; omitting the title
preserves its name. Saved apps appear before recents and survive restarts.
Use mini-browser agent apps to list saved tiles and mini-browser agent remove-app
URL to remove one. These operations require no page ID.
.PP
mini-browser mcp provides native MCP over stdio for Codex. Register it with:
.PP
.B codex mcp add mini_browser -- mini-browser mcp
.PP
Start the GUI separately with --agent. Control uses a private Unix socket,
not a TCP debugging port. MINI_BROWSER_AGENT_SOCKET overrides the default
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/mini-browser-agent/control.sock. The socket directory must be
owned by the current user with mode 0700. Raw CDP and page JavaScript provide
development access to websites and their sessions. Password dialogs and the
encrypted vault have no agent interface.
.PP
See docs/user/agents.md for the full command reference, compatibility boundaries,
and isolated UI tests (./scripts/smoke --test=agent).
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+L
Open the address and search dialog.
.TP
.B Alt+Home
Return to the home page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open Settings.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N / Ctrl+W
Open a new window / close the current window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R / F5
Refresh the current page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+R / Ctrl+F5
Reload without cached resources, keeping cookies and website storage.
.TP
.B Alt+Left / Alt+Right
Navigate back / forward.
.TP
.B F10
Reveal and focus the media title bar.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+I
Import Chrome bookmarks and history.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Manage the encrypted password vault and import Chrome password CSV files.
New vaults use an exactly six-digit PIN. Existing vaults accept their old
master password, which can be changed to a PIN in the Passwords dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+L
Choose and fill a saved login for the current website.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+K
Lock the password vault.
.TP
.B F1
Show all keyboard shortcuts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mini-browser/
Personal library, encrypted vault, cookies, and website data.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/mini-browser/
Website cache.
.PP
XDG_DATA_HOME and XDG_CACHE_HOME override the default data and cache roots.
.SH SEE ALSO
Documentation is installed in /usr/share/doc/mini-browser/.
